      "description": "Watch Seattle Sounders FC vs Chicago Fire highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The MLS spotlight shone brightly on the clash between Seattle Sounders FC and Chicago Fire FC , as both sides looked to climb the Western and Eastern Conference standings. This highly anticipated fixture, held on August 29, 2026 , delivered a tactical masterclass and a clinical display of finishing from both sets of attackers. Joveljic Sets the Pace The home crowd didn't have to wait long for the opening goal. In the 12th minute, Sebastian Gomez provided a perfectly weighted pass for Dejan Joveljic , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. Seattle's early dominance forced Chicago to rethink their strategy, and the visitors eventually found their rhythm late in the first half. In the 39th minute, the clinical Robert Lewandowski turned provider, setting up Maren Haile-Selassie for a crucial equalizer that sent the teams into the break on level terms. A Dramatic Second Half Turn Immediately after the restart, the Seattle Sounders FC regained the lead. Albert Rusnak 's vision in the 48th minute allowed Dejan Joveljic to net his second goal of the match, sending the stadium into a frenzy. The game's intensity grew, leading to a yellow card for Snyder Brunell shortly before a flurry of tactical substitutions from both managers. Managers brought on fresh legs like Jordan Morris and Jonathan Bamba to tip the scales in the final quarter of the match. Chicago's persistence finally paid off in the 82nd minute. Substitute Puso Dithejane made an instant impact by assisting Robert Lewandowski , who coolly converted to level the score once more. Despite a tense six minutes of stoppage time, neither side could find a winner, and the referee blew the final whistle on a captivating encounter that showcased the very best of American soccer."
